From 6cb42a1d028977f59e94af11b6a2a06f321704ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:44:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Build the Telegram Mini App on GitHub Pages

A Mini App is a web page, not a server, which is why it fits this architecture:
the daily run writes a static JSON feed, Pages serves the page, nothing runs in
between.

The existing nse_miniapp.html is left alone. It was written for the V1 scanner
shape -- situation, weekly_tier, strike, acc_days -- none of which exists in the
V2/V3, Ladder or Hull output, and it loads no Telegram SDK, so it is a plain web
page rather than a Mini App. V1 is frozen, so this is a separate build.

v2/miniapp_feed.py
  Normalises all four scanners' run files into one flat item list, so the page
  has a single shape to render regardless of how the scanners' internals differ.
  Adding a fifth scanner is one adapter plus one line in SCANNER_SOURCES; the
  page needs no change.

  Two properties are deliberate and pinned by tests:
  * Absent data is omitted, never defaulted. A missing price renders as a dash,
    not 0.00, because a zero reads as real information.
  * Availability is kept distinct from stage, so a circuit-locked or merged
    symbol stays visible and clearly unbuyable rather than disappearing.

  It is defensive by construction: a corrupt or missing scanner file cannot empty
  the feed, and each scanner's own market date is carried so the page can warn
  when one has fallen behind the others.

docs/index.html
  Single file, no build step, no bundler, no CDN beyond Telegram's own SDK -- a
  test enforces that. Telegram theme and dark mode, haptics, filter chips by
  scanner and stage, tap for the full plan, TradingView link.

  Internal reason codes never reach the screen. STALE_SYMBOL_PRICE reads
  "Hasn't traded recently", TERMINAL_MERGER reads "Merged into another company",
  NOT_IN_CURRENT_NSE_UNIVERSE reads "Not a listed company (fund or ETF)". A test
  asserts every code has a translation, so adding a code without plain wording
  fails the build.

.github/workflows/pages.yml
  Publishes docs/ on pushes that touch it, and refuses to publish when the feed
  is missing or not valid JSON. Requires one setting: Pages source = GitHub
  Actions.

pipeline.yml builds and commits the feed after the scanners run. The step is
continue-on-error, so a feed problem can never fail the scan.

v2/scanner_notices.render_miniapp_link appends the link to the Ladder and Hull
Pine cards. MINI_APP_TELEGRAM_LINK (a BotFather /newapp link) opens inside
Telegram; MINI_APP_URL opens in the browser and is labelled as such. Neither set
means no link and nothing breaks. nse_output.py is untouched, but reads the same
MINI_APP_URL, so setting it repoints the old V1 button too.

Verified against the real store: 42 items from two scanners -- 25 Ladder, 17 Hull
Pine, 5 of them open positions. A node check confirmed every item field the page
reads is one the builder can emit.

docs/MINIAPP_SETUP.md covers the four setup steps and states the limits plainly:
end-of-day only, read-only, and the feed is publicly readable because the repo
is public.

Tests: 23 new. Suite 446 passed.
