@@ -0,0 +1,140 @@
+# Mini App — setup and how it works
+
+A Telegram Mini App is a web page, not a server. That is why this fits GitHub
+Actions: the daily run writes a static JSON file, GitHub Pages serves the page,
+and nothing needs to be running in between.
+
+```
+06:00 IST pipeline  ─┬─>  scanners write output/*_daily*.json
+                     └─>  scripts/build_miniapp_feed.py  ->  docs/data/feed.json
+                                                              (committed)
+                                        │
+                     push to main ──> pages.yml ──> GitHub Pages
+                                                        │
+                                          docs/index.html reads data/feed.json
+```
+
+The old `nse_miniapp.html` is untouched. It was built for the V1 scanner shape
+(`situation`, `weekly_tier`, `strike`) and uses no Telegram SDK, so it is a plain
+web page rather than a Mini App. V1 is frozen, so this is a separate build.
+
+---
+
+## Step 1 — Turn on GitHub Pages
+
+Repository → **Settings** → **Pages** → **Build and deployment** → Source:
+**GitHub Actions**.
+
+That is the only click required. `pages.yml` publishes `docs/` on every push to
+`main` that touches it, and refuses to publish if the feed is missing or is not
+valid JSON.
+
+Your URL will be:
+
+```
+https://jayeshsrathod.github.io/nse-scanner/
+```
+
+## Step 2 — Check it loads
+
+Open that URL in a normal browser first. You should see the scan with filter
+chips across the top. If you see "Could not load the scan", the feed has not been
+committed yet — run the pipeline once, or generate one locally:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/build_miniapp_feed.py
+```
+
+## Step 3 — Register it as a Mini App (optional but worth it)
+
+Without this, the link in your Telegram message opens the phone's browser. With
+it, the app opens *inside* Telegram.
+
+In **@BotFather**:
+
+```
+/newapp
+```
+
+- Choose the bot you want it attached to
+- **Title**: `NSE Scanner`
+- **Short description**: `Daily paper scan across all scanners`
+- **Photo**: 640×360
+- **Web App URL**: `https://jayeshsrathod.github.io/nse-scanner/`
+- **Short name**: `scan`
+
+You get back a link like `https://t.me/your_bot/scan`.
+
+## Step 4 — Point the messages at it
+
+Add one repository secret:
+
+| Secret | Value | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| `MINI_APP_TELEGRAM_LINK` | `https://t.me/your_bot/scan` | opens inside Telegram |
+| `MINI_APP_URL` | `https://jayeshsrathod.github.io/nse-scanner/` | opens in the browser |
+
+Set the Telegram one if you did Step 3. If neither is set, no link is added and
+nothing breaks. Pass whichever you use into the daily workflows alongside the
+existing `*_TELEGRAM_*` secrets.
+
+Setting `MINI_APP_URL` also happens to repoint the old V1 button, since
+`nse_output.py` reads the same variable.
+
+---
+
+## What the app shows
+
+Two rows of filters. The first picks a scanner, the second a stage.
+
+| Chip | Means |
+|---|---|
+| Holding | open paper positions |
+| Ready | a plan exists and entry is authorised |
+| Almost ready | a plan exists, a gate is outstanding |
+| Confirming | participation building, no plan yet |
+| Early | movement detected, observation only |
+| Can't buy | circuit-locked, merged, extended, or a fund |
+
+Tap any row for the full plan — buy zone, stop, targets, risk, and a chart link.
+
+At the bottom, **"Why stocks were skipped"** is collapsed by default and shows
+the gateway's reasons in plain words. Internal codes never reach the screen; a
+test enforces that every code has a translation.
+
+Two deliberate behaviours:
+
+- **Absent data is absent.** No price shows as `₹—`, not `₹0.00`. A test pins
+  this, because a zero would read as real information.
+- **A lagging scanner is called out.** If Hull Pine ran on an older session than
+  the Ladder, a banner says so rather than silently mixing dates.
+
+---
+
+## Limits, honestly
+
+- **End of day only.** No live prices. The feed changes once a day.
+- **Read-only.** Tapping cannot record a decision, because that needs something
+  listening on the other end. GitHub Actions cannot host a webhook.
+- **Your repo is public**, so `docs/data/feed.json` is publicly readable. It
+  already was — `telegram_last_scan.json` has been public all along. If you want
+  it private, Cloudflare Pages serves free from a private repo.
+- **Mini App origin rules tightened on 20 July 2026.** Serve the page from one
+  fixed domain; GitHub Pages satisfies this.
+
+---
+
+## Adding a fifth scanner
+
+One adapter in `v2/miniapp_feed.py`, one line in `SCANNER_SOURCES`. The page
+needs no change — it renders whatever the feed contains.
+
+## When the feed looks wrong
+
+```bash
+python scripts/build_miniapp_feed.py     # prints per-scanner status
+```
+
+`MISSING` means that scanner's run file was absent or unreadable. The feed is
+built defensively: one broken scanner cannot empty the others, and the build step
+is `continue-on-error`, so a feed problem can never fail the scan itself.
